@startuml
title Message flow
autonumber

participant "Mallory\n(malicious client)" as M
participant "Alice\n(client)" as A
participant "Server\n(HTTP + WebSocket feed)" as S
database "DB" as DB
participant "Bob\n(client)" as B

== Sending a message ==
A -> S : GET /keys/bob
S -> DB : SELECT public_key
DB --> S : bob's key
S --> A : bob's public key

A -> A : payload = {"from":"alice","text":"..."}\nC = encrypt(bob key, payload)\ntimestamp = now (ms)\nsig = sign(H(pad(from, 32) || timestamp || C))
A -> S : POST /messages {from, to: "bob", timestamp, ciphertext: C, signature: sig}
S -> S : check size and JSON shape
S -> DB : INSERT INTO messages (sender, recipient, timestamp, frame)
S --> A : 200

== Broadcast ==
note over M, B
  All clients keep a WebSocket open and receive every stored frame.
  Alice, Bob and Mallory all see the exact same feed.
end note
S ->> A : push frame
S ->> B : push frame
S ->> M : push frame

A -> A : to != alice, drop\n(echo of own frame)
M -> M : to != mallory, drop\n(still keeps a copy of the ciphertext)

B -> B : to == bob
B -> S : GET /keys/alice
S --> B : alice's public key
B -> B : verify signature
B -> B : decrypt ciphertext
B -> B : parse payload strictly
B -> B : payload.from == frame.from ?
B -> B : display, ordered by timestamp
@enduml
